# Headers of the static pages (Workers static assets, developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/).
# The pages whose scripts ask the Worker for a signed-in reader hold a session's CSRF token: no other
# site may frame them, and they run this site's own files only (no inline script or style: Astro
# writes every script as a file, astro.config.mjs). The account page (Phase 5); /submit/, /removal/ and a
# paper's page (Phase 6), which holds the Code ↔ Paper reader since 2026-09-28: its browser reads the
# paper's text from Europe PMC (www.ebi.ac.uk, connect-src), else PubMed Central's copy (NCBI's
# E-utilities, eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov), and nothing else outside the site.
# worker/pages.ts gives the pages it renders the same headers (a test checks that they agree).
# The GitHub side (night phase 01): the pages that start an authorized action (/new/, /new/link/,
# /new/import/, /repositories/), the callback page of GitHub's authorization (/forge/authorized/: no
# Referer at all, so the code in its address never leaves), and the repository pages (/r/*), which
# also read GitHub's anonymous API and raw files in the reader's browser, on the reader's own quota
# (D00-5). Phase 02: the repository's own images are read as bytes and shown from object URLs
# (img-src blob:); no image loads from another host (D02-6), and nothing a repository holds runs
# (script-src 'self' only). Phase 05: the research issues' shell (/research/*) asks this site only
# (the Worker, the nightly shards).
/account/
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin

